{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"erratic-verminous-arrowworm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Scope: `src/rebar/llm/**` excluding plan_review and workflow — the package root plus code_review, prompting, review_kernel, evals, criteria, overlap. ~218 lines leave.\n\nContains the repo's #1 hotspot: `runner.py` 797/800, 88 commits, 12 in five days, with a 371-line method at its C901 ceiling. Recovering ~45 lines takes headroom from 3 to ~48 — roughly 4-5 stories of runway WITHOUT another split. ADR 0056 measured prose at 40% of `run()` and 50% of its pre-call region.\n\nA self-contradicting module: THREE sites assert Anthropic 400s when extended thinking meets a native output constraint, while `structured.py:228-238` — 210 lines below one of them, in the same file — explicitly calls that 'a stale rationale' and 'a relic'.\n\nA dead field found via its own comment: `runner.py:94-97` says `extra_tools` 'is always None in practice'; grep confirms no caller sets it. Delete the field, not the comment.\n\nConfirmed exemplar for the maintainer's original finding: `capabilities.py:166-198` is structurally a complete ADR (security posture for a BLOCKING gate, three numbered bounds, an explicitly accepted limitation on domain controls) and NO ADR in the 83-file corpus mentions web search in any form.\n\n85 lines are free wins — history already citing b690, b300, 2682, 3a98, 7a79, e3cd, 8455. `providers.py:3-16` duplicates ADR 0059 §1 verbatim including its file:line citations.\n\ncapabilities.py:295-316 is a matrix that cost real AWS accounts to produce and says so; capabilities.py:269-281 carries a rejected-alternative warning sitting exactly where the next reader would reintroduce it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured-fact and anti-refactor warnings stay verbatim","id":"4b94-8734-b8f5-42b7","parent_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","priority":3,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: llm core"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047092937110001,"uuid":"5390da70-a241-445f-ac99-ffb0c584b5dc"}